258
00:24:03,468 --> 00:24:04,803
I should've played
the proper villain.

259
00:25:11,078 --> 00:25:12,371
What's gotten into you?

260
00:25:15,624 --> 00:25:17,626
I couldn't even reach you.

261
00:25:53,704 --> 00:25:57,124
Pour it. I'll down it again anyway.

262
00:26:06,466 --> 00:26:07,467
Seong-wook said...

263
00:26:09,636 --> 00:26:10,846
he needed money.

264
00:26:14,891 --> 00:26:16,643
He said it was miserable
to be with me.

265
00:26:20,689 --> 00:26:22,607
How could I have been so blind
until it was too late?

266
00:26:25,277 --> 00:26:26,903
I always fail to notice
the people around me...

267
00:26:30,574 --> 00:26:32,409
falling apart.

268
00:26:40,000 --> 00:26:41,001
It was the same with my mom.

269
00:26:45,005 --> 00:26:46,089
I'm home.

270
00:26:59,352 --> 00:27:00,395
Mom?

271
00:27:03,065 --> 00:27:04,066
Mom...

272
00:27:09,780 --> 00:27:11,281
<i>My dad left home...</i>

273
00:27:13,283 --> 00:27:14,785
<i>and never came back.</i>

274
00:27:29,883 --> 00:27:31,093
<i>I thought</i>

275
00:27:32,511 --> 00:27:33,845
<i>things would get better with time.</i>

276
00:27:44,189 --> 00:27:45,607
<i>That she'd be okay</i>

277
00:27:47,317 --> 00:27:48,318
<i>because she had me.</i>

278
00:27:50,987 --> 00:27:52,197
<i>But I was wrong.</i>

279
00:28:04,543 --> 00:28:05,544
Mom.

280
00:28:30,527 --> 00:28:31,570
Mom!

281
00:28:49,838 --> 00:28:51,423
I was completely useless.

282
00:28:55,969 --> 00:28:57,554
Why aren't you watching
where you're going?

283
00:28:57,637 --> 00:28:59,723
Why did you cross the road
without checking the traffic light?

284
00:29:06,104 --> 00:29:07,397
I'm always too late.

285
00:29:11,943 --> 00:29:13,528
I end up driving everyone away.

286
00:29:20,202 --> 00:29:22,454
How is any of that your fault?

287
00:29:22,704 --> 00:29:24,122
They were hurting so much...

288
00:29:27,500 --> 00:29:28,919
and I failed to see it.

289
00:29:32,380 --> 00:29:34,758
I don't think I deserve
to have anyone by my side.

290
00:29:39,971 --> 00:29:41,181
At first

291
00:29:42,182 --> 00:29:44,684
I thought you were so cold.

292
00:29:46,686 --> 00:29:47,979
But now, I know.

293
00:29:49,648 --> 00:29:51,024
You aren't cold.

294
00:29:54,486 --> 00:29:55,737
You're just terrified.

295
00:29:59,324 --> 00:30:00,575
Terrified of losing people again.

296
00:30:02,285 --> 00:30:03,495
Terrified of being too late.

297
00:30:07,582 --> 00:30:09,751
When things get tough,
it's okay to admit it.

298
00:30:10,168 --> 00:30:13,463
It's okay to let yourself
fall apart sometimes.

299
00:30:16,633 --> 00:30:18,843
I'll stay by your side to the end.

300
00:30:21,846 --> 00:30:23,974
If I mean anything to you...

301
00:30:26,685 --> 00:30:27,978
don't let me go this time.

302
00:31:03,569 --> 00:31:05,738
<i>Hi, Mi-mi. Have you been busy lately?</i>

303
00:31:05,821 --> 00:31:07,990
<i>How about we go for a drive
this weekend? Are you in?</i>

304
00:31:08,073 --> 00:31:09,408
<i>Did I get dumped?</i>

305
00:31:09,491 --> 00:31:11,160
<i>I thought we really clicked that day.</i>

306
00:31:11,243 --> 00:31:13,662
<i>To find myself</i>

307
00:31:13,746 --> 00:31:16,123
<i>Lost in childhood dreams</i>

308
00:31:16,206 --> 00:31:17,958
<i>I'll go away</i>

309
00:31:18,042 --> 00:31:19,585
<i>Beyond the blue sky</i>

310
00:31:22,671 --> 00:31:23,756
Jeez.

311
00:31:25,132 --> 00:31:26,300
Goodness.

312
00:31:27,468 --> 00:31:29,553
Leaving someone on read
has its limits.

313
00:31:29,636 --> 00:31:31,388
If you play hard to get,
you'll end up getting played.

314
00:31:31,472 --> 00:31:34,224
This is how I keep them
thinking about me all day.

315
00:31:34,308 --> 00:31:36,352
It reels them in even faster.

316
00:31:37,561 --> 00:31:39,229
Reel him in? Oh, please.

317
00:31:40,314 --> 00:31:41,857
You're the one who got reeled in.

318
00:31:41,940 --> 00:31:45,569
I'm not into guys
who give up this easily anyway.

319
00:31:45,652 --> 00:31:47,654
If it's bothering you that much

320
00:31:48,280 --> 00:31:49,406
text him first.

321
00:31:51,325 --> 00:31:52,326
Me?

322
00:31:53,160 --> 00:31:54,161
Why would I do that?

323
00:31:55,454 --> 00:31:57,247
You treat relationships like a game.

324
00:31:57,873 --> 00:31:58,957
No wonder you're single.

325
00:32:01,043 --> 00:32:02,586
QUICK DELIVERY

326
00:32:09,760 --> 00:32:13,639
<i>Do you know why you guys are hooked
like helpless fish caught in her net?</i>

327
00:32:14,014 --> 00:32:15,140
<i>It's the impatience.</i>

328
00:32:16,058 --> 00:32:17,142
<i>Your desperation.</i>

329
00:32:17,226 --> 00:32:18,894
Right, the impatience...

330
00:32:18,977 --> 00:32:20,729
I'm too desperate.

331
00:32:21,563 --> 00:32:22,815
My impatience.

332
00:32:22,898 --> 00:32:24,149
<i>Right when you're ready to give up</i>

333
00:32:24,233 --> 00:32:26,652
<i>she'll toss you
another crumb with a text message.</i>

334
00:32:31,323 --> 00:32:32,783
<i>What are you up to?</i>

335
00:32:32,866 --> 00:32:34,076
MI-MI

336
00:32:34,159 --> 00:32:36,453
<i>That's when you stop!</i>

337
00:32:36,995 --> 00:32:38,872
<i>Don't even open it. Don't reply.</i>

338
00:32:39,248 --> 00:32:41,125
- Why not?
<i>- Treat her exactly the same way.</i>

339
00:32:41,458 --> 00:32:42,501
The same way?

340
00:32:43,794 --> 00:32:44,837
Goodness.

341
00:32:48,257 --> 00:32:50,092
Gosh, what do I do?

342
00:33:07,151 --> 00:33:09,278
My beloved Appello family.

343
00:33:12,281 --> 00:33:14,950
A lot has been going on
at our company lately.

344
00:33:15,242 --> 00:33:17,161
I'm sure most of you have guessed

345
00:33:18,203 --> 00:33:19,705
but we are

346
00:33:20,747 --> 00:33:23,750
- in a crisis right now.
- What crisis?

347
00:33:23,834 --> 00:33:26,378
With both our CEO
and our Planning Team Manager absent

348
00:33:26,462 --> 00:33:29,840
who are we supposed to rely on?

349
00:33:29,923 --> 00:33:34,511
In times like these,
we must stick together.

350
00:33:34,595 --> 00:33:38,640
We must protect the Appello we love.

351
00:33:38,724 --> 00:33:40,517
So who do we need right now?

352
00:33:42,019 --> 00:33:47,191
From here on out,
bring all important matters to me.

353
00:33:47,274 --> 00:33:49,860
For anything important,
you can rely on me.

354
00:33:49,943 --> 00:33:51,069
If you have any...

355
00:33:53,280 --> 00:33:54,448
Hello, Mr. Kang.

356
00:33:54,948 --> 00:33:56,158
You're here, Mr. Kang.

357
00:33:58,285 --> 00:34:01,663
- Thanks, but I'm here now.
- Why...

358
00:34:01,747 --> 00:34:02,748
I'm glad you're here.

359
00:34:06,418 --> 00:34:09,046
Shall we all get to work?

360
00:34:09,129 --> 00:34:10,255
- Yes!
- Yes!

361
00:34:13,550 --> 00:34:14,718
I meant well.

362
00:34:48,544 --> 00:34:50,128
HAN'S OFFICIAL KOREAN PARTNER

363
00:34:50,212 --> 00:34:51,838
APPELLO WAS CHOSEN
AS HAN'S OFFICIAL PARTNER IN KOREA

364
00:34:53,048 --> 00:34:54,049
We got it.

365
00:34:54,716 --> 00:34:55,926
No way!

366
00:34:56,969 --> 00:34:58,053
Check your email!

367
00:34:58,136 --> 00:34:59,763
- Did you see the notice?
- Yes!

368
00:34:59,846 --> 00:35:01,014
Did we get it?

369
00:35:03,100 --> 00:35:04,768
Great job, everyone.

370
00:35:05,561 --> 00:35:07,062
Congratulations.

371
00:35:14,653 --> 00:35:17,823
HAN'S OFFICIAL KOREAN PARTNER

372
00:35:17,906 --> 00:35:19,324
HAN, FASHION'S HOTTEST ISSUE

373
00:35:19,408 --> 00:35:21,243
{\an8}SIGNS MOU
WITH THEIR KOREAN PARTNER, APPELLO

374
00:35:21,326 --> 00:35:22,369
SE: ON, GREAT LOSS
ON UPFRONT INVESTMENT

375
00:35:22,452 --> 00:35:24,037
{\an8}FAILED TO WIN OVER HAN,
SE CORP. MIGHT LOSE BILLIONS

376
00:35:24,371 --> 00:35:26,039
{\an8}SE: ON USERS, MASSIVE EXODUS

377
00:35:26,123 --> 00:35:27,249
Kim Han-cheol!

378
00:35:27,332 --> 00:35:28,667
SE CORPORATION

379
00:35:28,750 --> 00:35:31,461
Do you know how much we lost
because of you?

380
00:35:31,545 --> 00:35:33,171
- I'm sorry, sir.
- Whatever.

381
00:35:33,255 --> 00:35:34,756
I won't renew your contract.

382
00:35:36,508 --> 00:35:38,802
- Sir.
- Jeez.

383
00:35:52,441 --> 00:35:55,902
I hope we get on well together,
Mr. Kang, my Korean business partner.

384
00:35:58,447 --> 00:35:59,573
Thanks, Jeong-yeon.

385
00:36:00,115 --> 00:36:01,366
You helped a great deal.

386
00:36:03,285 --> 00:36:05,662
Director Kim's career is over.

387
00:36:07,456 --> 00:36:10,208
Our joint operation
worked pretty well, right?

388
00:36:11,126 --> 00:36:12,169
Yes.

389
00:36:13,754 --> 00:36:15,922
- Are you going back to France?
- Yes.

390
00:36:16,381 --> 00:36:18,717
I'll prepare the launch
as soon as I get back.

391
00:36:19,051 --> 00:36:21,303
I'm serious about the Korean market.

392
00:36:22,512 --> 00:36:24,598
I'll work hard
so everything works out smoothly.

393
00:36:24,723 --> 00:36:27,434
Can you send
one of your staff to France?

394
00:36:27,976 --> 00:36:28,977
Sure.

395
00:36:36,568 --> 00:36:37,736
By the way

396
00:36:38,904 --> 00:36:40,489
I still don't get it.

397
00:36:40,906 --> 00:36:43,408
Why did SE Corporation
copy the fake presentation?

398
00:36:44,951 --> 00:36:48,288
You said you gave Mr. Choi
the actual proposal.

399
00:36:52,209 --> 00:36:53,210
I have no idea.

400
00:36:54,586 --> 00:36:56,171
I'd like to know too.

401
00:37:04,971 --> 00:37:06,264
Ms. Han.

402
00:37:15,232 --> 00:37:18,652
Can you spare me some time?

403
00:37:21,530 --> 00:37:25,617
NOT A CUSTOMER BUT A FAN
TASTEFUL SPACES IN KOREA

404
00:37:31,623 --> 00:37:34,209
When did you prepare all this?

405
00:37:35,544 --> 00:37:39,381
I threw together some ideas I had
while working on the proposal.

406
00:37:39,840 --> 00:37:42,718
These aren't just some ideas
thrown together.

407
00:37:46,263 --> 00:37:50,767
I'm a huge fan of your brand,
so I did it out of admiration.

408
00:37:53,562 --> 00:37:58,233
I also felt bad keeping you in check.

409
00:38:02,529 --> 00:38:06,283
- Do you have plans for today?
- Me? No.

410
00:38:06,825 --> 00:38:08,285
Then have dinner with me.

411
00:38:11,121 --> 00:38:12,247
I should pay you back.

412
00:38:14,166 --> 00:38:15,500
What food do you prefer?

413
00:38:16,334 --> 00:38:19,838
I eat pretty much anything.
What about you?

414
00:38:20,881 --> 00:38:23,759
- Korean cuisine.
- Korean cuisine...

415
00:38:25,719 --> 00:38:29,306
Would you like to try a place
I recommend?

416
00:38:38,940 --> 00:38:40,692
- It's hot.
- Thanks.

417
00:38:46,156 --> 00:38:49,701
They're all dishes my mom sent.

418
00:38:50,118 --> 00:38:52,204
She's an incredible cook.

419
00:38:54,122 --> 00:38:55,207
I'll enjoy this.

420
00:38:55,707 --> 00:38:57,334
I've been craving a home-cooked meal.

421
00:38:59,669 --> 00:39:03,381
You don't have family here, do you?

422
00:39:06,802 --> 00:39:07,928
In my senior year of high school

423
00:39:09,054 --> 00:39:11,890
I went abroad to study alone
because my mom remarried.

424
00:39:12,390 --> 00:39:14,267
I didn't want to live
with my stepdad.

425
00:39:17,187 --> 00:39:18,438
We don't keep in touch now.

426
00:39:21,399 --> 00:39:23,235
Being alone must've been tough.

427
00:39:24,277 --> 00:39:26,071
But I didn't struggle
financially, though.

428
00:39:27,239 --> 00:39:29,908
- Thanks for the meal.
- I hope you like it.

429
00:39:34,871 --> 00:39:36,498
- It's good.
- Isn't it?

430
00:39:36,581 --> 00:39:37,749
Please enjoy.

431
00:39:44,297 --> 00:39:45,298
It's tasty.

432
00:39:50,804 --> 00:39:55,267
At first, my only goal
was to become the best employee.

433
00:39:56,268 --> 00:39:59,813
Once I got started,
I found myself trying to find my way.

434
00:39:59,896 --> 00:40:02,357
It'll become clearer with time.

435
00:40:04,359 --> 00:40:07,112
You said last time

436
00:40:07,195 --> 00:40:11,825
that after your first brand failed,
you clearly saw what you could do.

437
00:40:13,326 --> 00:40:16,788
That stayed with me for a long time.

438
00:40:17,789 --> 00:40:21,209
I plan to try whatever I can
and make failures too.

439
00:40:22,419 --> 00:40:23,420
That's a great idea.

440
00:40:28,884 --> 00:40:32,971
I can see why Ha-gi chose you.

441
00:40:36,016 --> 00:40:38,810
You're comforting
like a home-cooked meal.

442
00:40:39,519 --> 00:40:40,520
And warm too.

443
00:40:43,565 --> 00:40:44,691
I am?

444
00:40:46,192 --> 00:40:48,612
Ha-gi's a great guy for seeing that.

445
00:40:51,197 --> 00:40:52,407
Enough that I want to steal him.

446
00:40:54,576 --> 00:40:55,702
Sorry?

447
00:40:57,287 --> 00:40:58,538
So keep him close.

448
00:41:04,210 --> 00:41:05,378
You scared me.

449
00:41:50,048 --> 00:41:51,049
Mom.

450
00:41:53,134 --> 00:41:54,636
You liked this coffee brand.

451
00:41:58,223 --> 00:41:59,557
For my sake...

452
00:42:02,143 --> 00:42:03,979
will you come and have a sip?

453
00:42:16,992 --> 00:42:18,952
I got your favorite.

454
00:42:20,495 --> 00:42:22,622
Why didn't you call ahead?

455
00:42:23,623 --> 00:42:26,710
I was passing by and thought of you.

456
00:42:29,087 --> 00:42:30,255
Let's go inside. I'm starving.

457
00:42:39,305 --> 00:42:40,640
It's the anniversary
of my mom's passing.

458
00:42:42,892 --> 00:42:43,893
This is your first time, right?

459
00:42:49,232 --> 00:42:50,400
You're such a jerk.

460
00:42:56,614 --> 00:42:58,783
Have you been doing this alone
without a word to me?

461
00:43:53,213 --> 00:43:54,214
I had no idea...

462
00:43:56,966 --> 00:43:59,594
how much you suffered after I left.

463
00:44:06,851 --> 00:44:08,353
Sorry for keeping it from you.

464
00:44:11,523 --> 00:44:12,690
I guess...

465
00:44:15,360 --> 00:44:17,445
I wasn't ready to face it myself.

466
00:44:20,740 --> 00:44:23,827
But thanks to Ms. Da-reum

467
00:44:25,411 --> 00:44:26,704
I've changed my mind.

468
00:44:28,414 --> 00:44:29,791
I've decided to protect what's mine.

469
00:44:32,335 --> 00:44:33,503
Everyone else has gone.

470
00:44:36,548 --> 00:44:37,924
But I really don't want to lose...

471
00:44:39,968 --> 00:44:41,386
both you and Ms. Da-reum.

472
00:45:01,865 --> 00:45:03,491
I hate myself.

473
00:45:06,494 --> 00:45:07,787
I'm nothing compared to you.

474
00:45:13,877 --> 00:45:15,044
You two

475
00:45:16,629 --> 00:45:17,922
mean a lot to me too.

476
00:45:21,634 --> 00:45:22,802
So...

477
00:45:26,806 --> 00:45:28,433
Make Da-reum happy.

478
00:45:56,794 --> 00:45:59,047
You'd better call me
for next year's anniversary.

479
00:46:00,465 --> 00:46:02,800
- I feel left out.
- Okay.

480
00:46:18,149 --> 00:46:19,943
<i>This is the contract
to Director Park's film.</i>

481
00:46:20,276 --> 00:46:21,361
<i>Congratulations, Chan.</i>

482
00:46:43,508 --> 00:46:45,927
ACTOR: LEE CHAN

483
00:46:50,014 --> 00:46:53,851
Whatever choice you make,
I want you to do

484
00:46:54,978 --> 00:46:56,312
what your heart tells you to do.

485
00:46:57,021 --> 00:46:58,731
<i>Something for yourself.</i>

486
00:47:08,491 --> 00:47:10,451
{\an8}TEO

487
00:47:10,535 --> 00:47:12,412
{\an8}<i>We've been practicing together.</i>

488
00:47:12,912 --> 00:47:15,540
{\an8}<i>Drop by if you'd like to see us.</i>

489
00:47:31,723 --> 00:47:33,224
I guess I'm not over it.

490
00:47:34,225 --> 00:47:35,268
Not yet.

491
00:47:55,079 --> 00:47:56,164
Chan.

492
00:48:09,385 --> 00:48:10,595
Thanks a lot.

493
00:48:10,845 --> 00:48:13,931
I didn't think you'd actually visit.

494
00:48:17,810 --> 00:48:20,313
Why are you here? To cheer us on?

495
00:48:23,775 --> 00:48:25,193
There's still something
I'd like to do.

496
00:48:30,573 --> 00:48:32,825
- Are we your sentimental backdrop?
- Don't.

497
00:48:32,909 --> 00:48:35,620
What could you still want
when you were the first to leave?

498
00:48:38,623 --> 00:48:40,208
We never waited for you.

499
00:48:50,718 --> 00:48:52,512
Then why did you leave
my part vacant?

500
00:48:58,309 --> 00:48:59,769
I get that you resent me.

501
00:49:00,520 --> 00:49:01,562
But

502
00:49:02,730 --> 00:49:03,898
I'm done running away.

503
00:49:05,483 --> 00:49:07,151
I know I'm asking a lot from you

504
00:49:08,736 --> 00:49:09,862
but one more time...

505
00:49:11,447 --> 00:49:12,657
Why don't we try again together

506
00:49:14,117 --> 00:49:15,910
just one more time?

507
00:49:22,750 --> 00:49:23,793
Together?

508
00:49:25,628 --> 00:49:27,880
Let's start again together.

509
00:49:29,799 --> 00:49:30,800
Chan.

510
00:49:38,099 --> 00:49:39,100
Okay?

511
00:49:49,318 --> 00:49:50,361
Come on.

512
00:49:55,950 --> 00:49:57,118
Darn it.

513
00:49:58,870 --> 00:50:00,746
Jeez.

514
00:50:20,349 --> 00:50:22,977
Why did you cancel my membership
when I still had classes left?

515
00:50:24,812 --> 00:50:25,980
You make me feel uncomfortable.

516
00:50:27,607 --> 00:50:29,650
- How so?
- You just do.

517
00:50:30,693 --> 00:50:31,777
I don't want to waste my energy.

518
00:50:33,863 --> 00:50:35,281
Let's call it quits, then.

519
00:50:37,074 --> 00:50:38,993
I'm done playing hard to get.

520
00:50:40,369 --> 00:50:42,663
I'm capable and competent,
and I'm a good kisser.

521
00:50:42,747 --> 00:50:45,041
- I'm pretty good at it.
- What are you on about?

522
00:50:45,541 --> 00:50:48,753
I'll call when I want
and come to see you when I want.

523
00:50:51,589 --> 00:50:52,590
You win.

524
00:50:53,633 --> 00:50:54,842
I lost.

525
00:50:56,052 --> 00:50:58,804
You should quit playing games
and do the same.

526
00:50:59,096 --> 00:51:00,097
Sorry?

527
00:51:01,140 --> 00:51:02,141
What do you mean?

528
00:51:04,936 --> 00:51:05,978
Let's date.

529
00:51:34,090 --> 00:51:38,761
Don't you miss the other D.N.X guys?

530
00:51:41,389 --> 00:51:43,099
Would they miss me?

531
00:51:47,562 --> 00:51:49,522
I wouldn't know.

532
00:52:24,640 --> 00:52:26,809
Can I help you?

533
00:52:27,977 --> 00:52:29,437
- I brought your food.
- I see.

534
00:52:30,062 --> 00:52:31,856
Can you leave it over there?

535
00:52:32,607 --> 00:52:33,649
Sure.

536
00:52:34,358 --> 00:52:36,902
What about Roy's part?

537
00:52:39,071 --> 00:52:41,907
- Let's forget about it.
- He might come back.

538
00:52:42,158 --> 00:52:43,200
How?

539
00:52:43,576 --> 00:52:45,119
We don't even know
if he's dead or alive.

540
00:52:45,202 --> 00:52:46,329
He can't be dead.

541
00:52:51,500 --> 00:52:52,668
What if we look for him?

542
00:53:16,359 --> 00:53:17,610
You feel like

543
00:53:17,693 --> 00:53:21,238
you shouldn't meet the members,
even though you miss them, right?

544
00:53:23,074 --> 00:53:24,158
Is it because you feel bad?

545
00:53:26,202 --> 00:53:27,370
I ruined everything.

546
00:53:28,329 --> 00:53:29,622
That would be too shameless.

547
00:53:30,581 --> 00:53:32,708
Then go and show them how you feel.

548
00:53:34,752 --> 00:53:37,380
You can show
that you feel embarrassed

549
00:53:38,214 --> 00:53:39,507
or you could even cry.

550
00:53:41,425 --> 00:53:42,760
Why decide on your own?

551
00:53:44,011 --> 00:53:46,430
You don't know
if they'll curse you out

552
00:53:46,806 --> 00:53:49,058
or yell or take you back.

553
00:53:54,105 --> 00:53:55,106
I'm afraid.

554
00:54:06,117 --> 00:54:09,078
Do you know why I started deliveries
just to track you down?

555
00:54:11,914 --> 00:54:14,083
The thought of never seeing you again
and regretting it...

556
00:54:16,502 --> 00:54:19,422
was far scarier than the thought

557
00:54:20,548 --> 00:54:22,341
of getting disappointed
after meeting you.

558
00:54:24,719 --> 00:54:27,012
Your members might feel the same.

559
00:54:27,555 --> 00:54:31,225
They might hate you
but still miss you.

560
00:54:33,102 --> 00:54:34,603
If you really feel bad

561
00:54:36,564 --> 00:54:38,274
stop hiding

562
00:54:39,358 --> 00:54:41,986
and give the guys
a chance to hate you.

563
00:54:56,584 --> 00:54:59,128
I could cook better
if I had cookbooks.

564
00:54:59,837 --> 00:55:02,506
- Shall I buy you a few?
- No, thanks.

565
00:55:03,132 --> 00:55:05,134
MAGAZINE

566
00:55:08,429 --> 00:55:09,430
Wait.

567
00:55:12,725 --> 00:55:13,976
{\an8}It's Ms. Han.

568
00:55:19,315 --> 00:55:20,775
I guess she gave an interview
while she was here.

569
00:55:23,819 --> 00:55:26,739
- Shall we go?
- Hold on. Let me read a bit more.

570
00:55:34,246 --> 00:55:36,791
{\an8}HAN AND HER QUESTIONS

571
00:55:39,710 --> 00:55:42,087
{\an8}A NEW ENVIRONMENT
BRINGS NEW QUESTIONS

572
00:55:42,171 --> 00:55:45,257
{\an8}THEY MADE ME STRONGER, FIRMER,
AND HELPED ME GROW

573
00:56:10,157 --> 00:56:11,784
Shall we go to the seaside
to watch the sun rise?

574
00:56:11,867 --> 00:56:14,078
I'd like that. Where would we go?

575
00:56:15,246 --> 00:56:17,414
We should go to the East Sea.

576
00:56:18,374 --> 00:56:20,084
Will we be
spending the night together?

577
00:56:22,920 --> 00:56:25,214
I guess so?

578
00:56:28,884 --> 00:56:29,885
A two-day trip?

579
00:56:38,644 --> 00:56:41,438
I really just want to see
the sunrise.

580
00:56:46,443 --> 00:56:47,570
I'll think about it.

581
00:56:49,780 --> 00:56:50,781
Okay.

582
00:56:51,866 --> 00:56:54,368
You should get inside.

583
00:56:54,660 --> 00:56:55,661
Okay.

584
00:57:06,589 --> 00:57:08,132
It's late. You should go.

585
00:57:09,800 --> 00:57:10,801
Okay.

586
00:57:13,762 --> 00:57:15,556
- I'll go.
- Okay.

587
00:57:18,559 --> 00:57:20,352
- I should go.
- Yes.

588
00:57:39,163 --> 00:57:40,414
Mr. Kang.

589
00:57:41,957 --> 00:57:44,001
- Yes?
- My place

590
00:57:44,877 --> 00:57:46,879
might not have cats

591
00:57:47,922 --> 00:57:49,214
but there's something interesting.

592
00:57:51,091 --> 00:57:52,092
Would you like to see it?

593
00:57:56,722 --> 00:57:58,557
Something interesting?

594
00:58:07,608 --> 00:58:08,817
What could it be?

595
00:58:11,153 --> 00:58:12,237
I'm nervous now.

596
00:58:16,617 --> 00:58:17,868
Let's see.

597
00:58:39,556 --> 00:58:41,350
Try not to be too shocked.

598
00:58:44,436 --> 00:58:46,063
- Why show me this?
- What?

599
00:58:46,146 --> 00:58:48,232
You said your underwear was in here.

600
00:58:49,400 --> 00:58:50,693
So why...

601
00:59:05,874 --> 00:59:07,001
Ta-da.

602
00:59:13,757 --> 00:59:15,467
I LOVE LEE CHAN

603
00:59:15,759 --> 00:59:17,261
What is...

604
00:59:18,137 --> 00:59:20,097
What is all this?

605
00:59:20,180 --> 00:59:21,640
ALWAYS ON CHAN'S SIDE
FOREVER LEE CHAN

606
00:59:21,724 --> 00:59:23,851
It's a record of my 12 years

607
00:59:24,476 --> 00:59:25,519
as a fan.

608
00:59:36,864 --> 00:59:39,116
I didn't want to hide it anymore.

609
00:59:40,534 --> 00:59:42,077
I wanted to show you
that this is who I am

610
00:59:42,911 --> 00:59:45,581
and the part of me that loves you

611
00:59:47,124 --> 00:59:48,333
is also a part of who I am.

612
00:59:54,757 --> 00:59:56,341
That's a weight off my shoulders.

613
00:59:56,759 --> 00:59:58,552
I can sleep at night at last.

614
01:00:01,305 --> 01:00:02,473
Gosh.

615
01:00:04,641 --> 01:00:05,976
What is it?

616
01:00:06,060 --> 01:00:10,230
You came clean first,
so I told you my secret too.

617
01:00:13,067 --> 01:00:14,401
I'm jealous, to be honest.

618
01:00:19,281 --> 01:00:21,283
I'll cut back on it now.

619
01:00:34,088 --> 01:00:36,256
I know he gave you
the will and energy to live.

620
01:00:39,176 --> 01:00:40,803
I should thank Chan.

621
01:00:44,807 --> 01:00:47,810
He brought us together.

622
01:00:52,397 --> 01:00:55,984
Does that mean my bias

623
01:00:57,402 --> 01:00:58,612
is you now?

624
01:01:58,839 --> 01:02:01,049
{\an8}- I'm heavy.
- Not at all.

625
01:03:45,779 --> 01:03:49,783
I used to have an olive lemon shot
and Greek yogurt for breakfast.

626
01:03:49,866 --> 01:03:51,034
I quit that diet.

627
01:03:51,660 --> 01:03:52,828
Why?

628
01:03:53,161 --> 01:03:55,789
Cutting down on carbs
left me with no energy.

629
01:03:57,374 --> 01:03:58,917
Eat as much as you want.

630
01:03:59,501 --> 01:04:00,669
You weigh too little.

631
01:04:07,884 --> 01:04:10,595
Stop staring at me.
It's embarrassing.

632
01:04:12,848 --> 01:04:14,141
What were you thinking about?

633
01:04:14,391 --> 01:04:15,851
Will you stop it?

634
01:04:17,894 --> 01:04:19,813
It's not the first time
we've slept together.

635
01:04:20,814 --> 01:04:22,858
What are you talking about?

636
01:04:22,941 --> 01:04:24,234
When did we ever...

637
01:04:25,861 --> 01:04:27,070
After the welcome dinner.

638
01:04:27,696 --> 01:04:28,822
In my office.

639
01:04:46,506 --> 01:04:49,301
I tried to stay up all night,
but ended up falling asleep.

640
01:04:50,344 --> 01:04:51,511
No wonder.

641
01:04:52,220 --> 01:04:54,222
It all felt a bit familiar.

642
01:05:00,562 --> 01:05:02,147
I really had no idea then

643
01:05:03,440 --> 01:05:04,733
that this would happen.

644
01:05:19,414 --> 01:05:21,041
HAN AND HER QUESTIONS

645
01:05:22,626 --> 01:05:23,710
{\an8}A NEW ENVIRONMENT
BRINGS NEW QUESTIONS

646
01:05:23,794 --> 01:05:25,170
{\an8}THEY MADE ME STRONGER, FIRMER,
AND HELPED ME GROW

647
01:05:38,141 --> 01:05:40,811
ANY ADVICE FOR YOUNGER DESIGNERS
OR THOSE FINDING THEIR WAY?

648
01:05:40,894 --> 01:05:45,816
DON'T TRY TOO HARD TO CHANGE YOURSELF
CHANGE WHERE YOU ARE

649
01:05:54,741 --> 01:05:55,742
Mr. Kang.

650
01:05:57,369 --> 01:05:58,370
Yes?

651
01:06:01,206 --> 01:06:02,249
How about

652
01:06:03,458 --> 01:06:07,003
I apply to work in Paris?

653
01:06:28,942 --> 01:06:32,487
{\an8}MY BIAS, MY BOSS

654
01:06:42,622 --> 01:06:44,833
{\an8}<i>I know it's a great opportunity
for Ms. Da-reum.</i>

655
01:06:45,584 --> 01:06:46,835
{\an8}But I want her to stay.

656
01:06:46,918 --> 01:06:48,920
{\an8}Long-distance relationships
never work out.

657
01:06:49,463 --> 01:06:50,505
{\an8}- Hey!
- My goodness!

658
01:06:50,589 --> 01:06:53,175
{\an8}<i>People there greet each other
with a kiss on the cheek.</i>

659
01:06:54,092 --> 01:06:55,093
{\an8}- One.
- Two.

660
01:06:55,177 --> 01:06:56,178
{\an8}- Three.
- Four.

661
01:06:56,261 --> 01:06:57,596
{\an8}- Five.
- Let's go!

662
01:06:57,679 --> 01:06:58,680
{\an8}Come back, Roy.

663
01:06:58,763 --> 01:07:01,141
{\an8}<i>Let's stop running away.</i>

664
01:07:01,224 --> 01:07:02,684
{\an8}<i>Instead of cheering you on</i>

665
01:07:03,101 --> 01:07:05,145
{\an8}I hated myself for feeling so petty.

666
01:07:06,396 --> 01:07:07,522
{\an8}<i>It felt like it was about me.</i>

667
01:07:07,689 --> 01:07:09,483
{\an8}<i>You may be saying it to your fans</i>

668
01:07:09,774 --> 01:07:12,360
{\an8}<i>but it's what I wanted to say to you.</i>

669
01:07:12,444 --> 01:07:13,612
{\an8}<i>You won't let go</i>

670
01:07:14,029 --> 01:07:15,739
{\an8}<i>just because I'm leaving, will you?</i>

671
01:07:18,868 --> 01:07:20,870
{\an8}Subtitles by Eunjin Erica Kim
and Jennifer Jean Lim

672
01:07:20,951 --> 01:07:22,953
